    <p style="font-size:13px;color:#D5D8DD;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;">ğŸ¤– <strong style="color:#F8F9FA;">What "Seal document with forensic report" does.</strong> Your document is analysed entirely on this device, in your browser, by the deterministic engine; its findings are stated as fact and anchored to quoted text on cited pages. Then the AI review runs on Cloudflare Workers AI: a short excerpt is classified for context, the findings are assessed before the report is built, <strong style="color:#F8F9FA;">Brain 9 reads the sealed page text</strong> (up to 16 windows of about 11,000 characters, pages without findings first) for anything the engine missed â€” every suggestion must quote the text verbatim or it is discarded â€” and the court-ready narrative is written section by section beside the technical report from the sealed page text, the findings JSON and the sealed technical report. The engine is the first extractor, not the limit of the narrative: a contradiction the engine missed can print only when both quoted sides verify against the cited sealed pages. Large bundles are supplied in a bounded, declared page set; the printed provenance states exactly what the narrator received. Brain 9 recommendations are shown here and held outside the sealed reports; the verdict on any person is for the court.</p>
